{"title":"Carmichael number","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Carmichael_numbers\">Carmichael numbers</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Carmichael_number&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Carmichael numbers\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>A <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">Carmichael number</a> is a <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Composite_number\" title=\"Composite number\">composite number</a> that satisfies <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Fermat%27s_Little_Theorem\" title=\"Fermat&#39;s Little Theorem\">Fermat's Little Theorem</a>, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/c/84c4d8c126197d4b655af8353982675772c1970b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a^p \\equiv a \\pmod{p}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"130\" height=\"20\" />or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/c/3/ec35da9872ebe1091ab3765495f6dec476d92a2d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a^{p - 1} \\equiv 1 \\pmod{p}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"147\" height=\"21\" /> In this case, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> is the Carmichael number.\n</p><p>The first <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/a/e0a0db32027a732ac57d37ef2ae9bb150f65b108.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> Carmichael numbers are:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/a/65ab6e503f0281b214e69f6ed79ea48cf4747bc8.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align} 561 &amp;= 3 \\cdot 11 \\cdot 17 \\\\ 1105 &amp;= 5 \\cdot 13 \\cdot 17 \\\\ 1729 &amp;= 7 \\cdot 13 \\cdot 19 \\\\ 2465 &amp;= 5 \\cdot 17 \\cdot 29 \\\\ 2821 &amp;= 7 \\cdot 13 \\cdot 31 \\\\ 6601 &amp;= 7 \\cdot 23 \\cdot 41 \\\\ 8991 &amp;= 7 \\cdot 19 \\cdot 67. \\end{align}\" width=\"306\" height=\"166\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Carmichael_number&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Fermat%27s_Little_Theorem\" title=\"Fermat&#39;s Little Theorem\">Fermat's Little Theorem</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Carmichael_function\" title=\"Carmichael function\">Carmichael function</a></li></ul>\n<p><br />\n~ <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=User:Enderramsby&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"User:Enderramsby (page does not exist)\">enderramsby</a>\n</p><p><br />\n<i>This article is a stub.  Help us out by <span class=\"plainlinks\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=Carmichael_number&amp;action=edit\">expanding it</a></span>.</i>\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017153811\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.010 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.017 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 39/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 292/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 4/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 1149/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    5.761      1 Template:Stub\n100.00%    5.761      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:22961:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017153811 and revision id 176640. Rendering was triggered because: page-view\n -->\n</div>"}